<h2>Rod-bend model — end-loaded vertical column</h2>
<div class="sub" style="max-width:68ch">Model assumption: each column's rod is vertical and
touched only at its two end mounts — no other applied force, and gravity acts axially. With no
lateral load along the span, an axially compressed pin-ended rod deflects as its mount line
plus a half-sine buckle: <span class="mono">d(s) = a + b·s + A·sin(πs)</span>, three parameters
per column. Residuals from that shape separate real geometry from sensor error.</div>

